  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Young activists creating space in LBN</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As part of The Socio-Economic Justice Initiative-MAAN  strategy to Build the accountability and citizen engagement culture, MAAN will develop and implement an &#x201c;Activist Academy&#x201d; for cross-regional Lebanese youth, to foster a culture of citizen accountability by building the capacity of young activists through workshops and engagement opportunities with other activists and practitioners. Utilizing our network of over 20 civil society experts, academics, and consultants, MAAN will outreach and select youthbetween the ages of 18-25 based on various criteria to commit and participate in the citizenship building sessions. The project aims to catalyze not only the interest amongst youth to engage, but also to capacitate their activism spirit to become more efficient, sustainable and resilient. The Academy agenda will consist of weekly workshops and seminars divided between knowledge and skills sessions targeting youth, to build a popular and public movement advocating for changes through policy development inLebanon. The lack of knowledge and tools is limiting the efficiency of their activism, hence the need to support the Lebanese youth and strengthen their knowledge and guide their activism to become more sustainable and resilient in their pursuit of an equitable system.</narrative>
  </description>
